1
00:00:01,393 --> 00:00:04,253
Previously on JoJo's Bizarre Adventure...

2
00:00:06,633 --> 00:00:08,910
Hey, old man. Something's off.

3
00:00:08,993 --> 00:00:10,930
You're going the wrong direction.

4
00:00:11,013 --> 00:00:11,843
Hmm?

5
00:00:11,973 --> 00:00:14,030
We seem to be heading toward that island.

6
00:00:14,113 --> 00:00:17,819
But before we arrive in Egypt,
we need to make a slight detour.

7
00:00:18,033 --> 00:00:20,386
Someone is waiting for us on the island.

8
00:00:21,513 --> 00:00:22,343
Hmm.

9
00:00:22,426 --> 00:00:25,171
He's a man who is extremely
important to our journey.

10
00:00:25,733 --> 00:00:27,513
What is that supposed to mean?

11
00:00:36,013 --> 00:00:37,753
Hey, what's the big idea?

12
00:00:38,093 --> 00:00:39,975
Does someone actually live here?

13
00:00:40,093 --> 00:00:43,490
This is such a tiny little
island, it's practically deserted.

14
00:00:43,573 --> 00:00:44,867
I would have to agree.

15
00:00:45,473 --> 00:00:46,303
Mr.

16
00:00:46,386 --> 00:00:48,510
Joestar, are you sure
someone actually lives here?

17
00:00:48,593 --> 00:00:51,122
He's been living on
this island by himself.

18
00:00:51,253 --> 00:00:54,590
A man told me back in India, and
I'm sure I heard him correctly.

19
00:00:54,673 --> 00:00:55,503
Wait a sec.

20
00:00:55,593 --> 00:00:57,993
When you say, a man... What?

21
00:00:58,353 --> 00:00:59,471
Mangoes from India?

22
00:01:00,453 --> 00:01:01,670
I

23
00:01:01,753 --> 00:01:08,753
don't

24
00:01:25,613 --> 00:01:26,443
know.

25
00:02:42,893 --> 00:02:44,069
I hate to interrupt,

26
00:02:44,233 --> 00:02:47,210
but I thought you should know someone's
watching us from the grass over there.

27
00:02:47,293 --> 00:02:48,123
What?

28
00:02:49,973 --> 00:02:50,803
Hey!

29
00:02:55,133 --> 00:02:56,630
From the back, he looks...

30
00:02:56,713 --> 00:02:57,543
You're right.

31
00:02:57,626 --> 00:02:58,613
I know that face.

32
00:03:02,193 --> 00:03:03,033
Hold on!

33
00:03:03,293 --> 00:03:04,133
Just wait!

34
00:03:13,433 --> 00:03:14,493
Eat up now!

35
00:03:14,793 --> 00:03:16,030
Are you hungry, Michael?

36
00:03:16,113 --> 00:03:17,407
How about you, Prince?

37
00:03:17,853 --> 00:03:22,450
I mixed in those shells you love, so make
sure you share with the others, alright?

38
00:03:22,533 --> 00:03:24,830
And there's lots more
where this came from.

39
00:03:24,913 --> 00:03:28,870
Make sure to get nice and fat so
you'll be a tasty chicken, Lionel.

40
00:03:28,953 --> 00:03:30,113
It's not possible.

41
00:03:30,533 --> 00:03:31,490
That man...

42
00:03:31,573 --> 00:03:33,773
It can't be. It's... Hold it!

43
00:03:35,253 --> 00:03:36,930
I'm gonna go and talk to him.

44
00:03:37,013 --> 00:03:39,307
The rest of you just wait here for now.

45
00:03:41,333 --> 00:03:43,509
Pardon me, my name is Joseph Joestar.

46
00:03:43,973 --> 00:03:47,490
My friends and I are currently
traveling on an expedition to Egypt...

47
00:03:47,573 --> 00:03:48,403
Go away!

48
00:03:48,486 --> 00:03:49,316
I won't hear it!

49
00:03:50,653 --> 00:03:52,170
His voice sounds like...

50
00:03:52,253 --> 00:03:53,613
I won't say it again!

51
00:03:53,813 --> 00:03:54,770
Don't talk to me!

52
00:03:54,853 --> 00:03:55,683
Got it?

53
00:03:55,766 --> 00:03:58,870
No one ever comes to see me when
they have actual good news to report.

54
00:03:58,953 --> 00:04:01,710
I only get visitors when
something bad happens!

55
00:04:01,793 --> 00:04:02,713
Just shut up!

56
00:04:02,973 --> 00:04:04,073
Go away!

57
00:04:04,973 --> 00:04:06,193
Mr. Avdol!

58
00:04:06,973 --> 00:04:08,793
Avdol, wait! I said go!

59
00:04:10,013 --> 00:04:10,953
Hold on!

60
00:04:11,193 --> 00:04:12,252
That's impossible!

61
00:04:12,553 --> 00:04:14,253
That wasn't Avdol.

62
00:04:14,693 --> 00:04:16,173
It was his father.

63
00:04:16,993 --> 00:04:18,013
His father?

64
00:04:19,293 --> 00:04:22,993
He withdrew from society and
lives alone on this island.

65
00:04:23,433 --> 00:04:26,390
I'm sorry that I wasn't able
to tell you about this earlier.

66
00:04:26,473 --> 00:04:30,533
But if it ever became known to
Dio that we stopped at this place,

67
00:04:31,193 --> 00:04:33,840
Avdahl's father would
be put in grave danger.

68
00:04:34,113 --> 00:04:36,913
I would never forgive
myself if that happened.

69
00:04:37,713 --> 00:04:43,013
But for now, my focus has to be on
telling him what every parent fears most.

70
00:04:43,673 --> 00:04:45,153
That his son is dead.

71
00:04:47,373 --> 00:04:48,513
Pull the rift!

72
00:05:00,413 --> 00:05:02,060
Don't let yourself go there.

73
00:05:02,193 --> 00:05:04,075
Avdol's death wasn't your fault.

74
00:05:07,993 --> 00:05:10,010
No, it's entirely my fault.

75
00:05:10,093 --> 00:05:12,853
I'll carry that burden
for as long as I live.

76
00:05:18,533 --> 00:05:21,353
Is it safe to assume his
father's a stand user?

77
00:05:22,453 --> 00:05:26,990
Yeah, but I don't know what kind of stand
it is or what sort of power it wields.

78
00:05:27,073 --> 00:05:29,370
Judging by the way his
father reacted to us,

79
00:05:29,453 --> 00:05:32,230
I doubt he'll offer us much
in the way of assistance.

80
00:05:32,313 --> 00:05:34,850
You just leave the
talking to me, all right?

81
00:05:34,933 --> 00:05:37,580
Hopefully my words will
be able to reach him.

82
00:05:55,913 --> 00:06:01,453
All I ever wanted was to avenge my sister's
death, and I ended up killing my friend.

83
00:06:01,973 --> 00:06:05,330
There's nothing I could possibly
do to make it up to his father.

84
00:06:05,413 --> 00:06:07,531
I'm between a rock and a hard place.

85
00:06:09,093 --> 00:06:10,473
Talk about depressing.

86
00:06:22,053 --> 00:06:22,883
Huh?

87
00:06:25,093 --> 00:06:26,713
This thing is pretty shiny.

88
00:06:27,353 --> 00:06:30,273
I wonder if it drifted
up from some sunken ship.

89
00:06:30,573 --> 00:06:32,514
Just look at all those barnacles.

90
00:06:33,053 --> 00:06:35,353
It's definitely made of metal, but...

91
00:06:37,433 --> 00:06:40,110
There's some kind of
creepy face carved on it.

92
00:06:40,193 --> 00:06:42,450
Despite that, it looks pretty valuable.

93
00:06:42,533 --> 00:06:46,651
Now if I can scratch off these
barnacles, we'll really be in business.

94
00:06:48,333 --> 00:06:49,473
What the hell?

95
00:06:57,513 --> 00:06:58,413
It's gone!

96
00:06:59,193 --> 00:07:01,453
What in the world happened just now?

97
00:07:01,733 --> 00:07:02,750
From the looks of it,

98
00:07:02,833 --> 00:07:06,833
the air trapped inside just burst
out and I was scared over nothing.

99
00:07:07,053 --> 00:07:07,883
Ooh.

100
00:07:08,193 --> 00:07:11,210
Luckily, I'm not dealing with
Aladdin's magic lamp or anything,

101
00:07:11,293 --> 00:07:13,175
so I guess I can relax a little.

102
00:07:15,473 --> 00:07:16,713
You get three!

103
00:07:17,993 --> 00:07:19,210
Three, I say!

104
00:07:19,293 --> 00:07:21,253
Your wish is my command!

105
00:07:21,673 --> 00:07:24,320
Three wishes for whatever
your heart desires!

106
00:07:24,773 --> 00:07:26,873
What sort of fresh hell is this?

107
00:07:27,253 --> 00:07:28,893
I am known as Cameo.

108
00:07:29,213 --> 00:07:32,110
Allow me to thank you for
freeing me from the lab.

109
00:07:32,193 --> 00:07:35,390
Tell me your three wishes so
that I might grant them for you.

110
00:07:35,473 --> 00:07:36,730
Hold it, you smoky freak!

111
00:07:36,813 --> 00:07:38,284
Are you a new stand user?

112
00:07:38,633 --> 00:07:40,053
Silver Chariots!

113
00:07:49,813 --> 00:07:50,643
Damn it.

114
00:07:50,933 --> 00:07:52,473
This guy's not half bad.

115
00:07:53,093 --> 00:07:54,493
What awesome power!

116
00:07:55,313 --> 00:07:59,590
Listen buddy, your strength tells me
that your user is definitely nearby.

117
00:07:59,673 --> 00:08:00,513
Now who is it?

118
00:08:00,733 --> 00:08:02,730
Would you like the answer to that question

119
00:08:02,813 --> 00:08:05,310
to be considered as your
first official wish?

120
00:08:05,393 --> 00:08:08,353
It's a little on the
boring side if you ask me.

121
00:08:08,953 --> 00:08:12,247
Don't pull that genie in a
bottle crap with me, fishier.

122
00:08:12,433 --> 00:08:15,830
But if you're saying you could make me
a super rich man right this instant,

123
00:08:15,913 --> 00:08:16,743
let's see it.

124
00:08:17,293 --> 00:08:18,890
Is that your first wish?

125
00:08:18,973 --> 00:08:20,233
Going once.

126
00:08:20,453 --> 00:08:24,890
Go ahead and grant it if you can, but
otherwise stop jerking me around, dammit!

127
00:08:24,973 --> 00:08:27,293
Then consider your wish granted. Huh?

128
00:08:27,793 --> 00:08:30,073
Hail to you!

129
00:08:45,033 --> 00:08:48,253
I don't understand a single
thing that just happened.

130
00:08:49,273 --> 00:08:52,633
So that strange guy wasn't
the enemy's stand after all.

131
00:08:52,953 --> 00:08:56,890
I thought he'd attack me, but instead
he told me to make three wishes.

132
00:08:56,973 --> 00:09:00,693
I don't know what's going on
here, but I don't trust that guy.

133
00:09:01,873 --> 00:09:04,053
Someone shady is on this island.

134
00:09:05,153 --> 00:09:07,613
It's probably a good idea to tell Mr.

135
00:09:07,793 --> 00:09:09,381
Joestar what happened here.

136
00:09:10,173 --> 00:09:14,526
There might be a chance it could have
something to do with Avdol's father.

137
00:09:15,313 --> 00:09:16,143
Huh?

138
00:09:17,993 --> 00:09:18,853
That's weird.

139
00:09:18,973 --> 00:09:21,855
What's up with all that
loud clanging back there?

140
00:09:27,853 --> 00:09:29,206
Whoa, is this for real?

141
00:09:29,353 --> 00:09:30,613
But it can't be!

142
00:09:34,333 --> 00:09:37,233
Wait, this is gold from
the Napoleonic era!

143
00:09:37,513 --> 00:09:39,593
This isn't a dream or an illusion!

144
00:09:39,913 --> 00:09:40,833
Holy crap!

145
00:09:41,253 --> 00:09:42,893
A treasure Drive of gold!

146
00:09:43,033 --> 00:09:45,739
I wouldn't believe it
if it wasn't right here!

147
00:09:46,393 --> 00:09:48,353
I don't get it! What is this?

148
00:09:48,453 --> 00:09:49,930
Are you mocking me or something?

149
00:09:50,013 --> 00:09:51,072
No, that's not it.

150
00:09:51,313 --> 00:09:52,753
He can't be mocking me.

151
00:09:52,933 --> 00:09:55,190
When could he have buried this gold here?

152
00:09:55,273 --> 00:09:58,790
There's no way he would have had
time to bury it after I made my wish.

153
00:09:58,873 --> 00:10:01,713
So how the hell did
that freak do all this?

154
00:10:02,513 --> 00:10:04,833
Now, what is your second wish?

155
00:10:05,533 --> 00:10:07,233
Your wish is my command.

156
00:10:07,633 --> 00:10:09,110
This doesn't make any sense.

157
00:10:09,193 --> 00:10:10,210
Why are you doing this?

158
00:10:10,293 --> 00:10:11,290
What are you scheming?

159
00:10:11,373 --> 00:10:13,970
You don't think I'd fall
for your stupid tricks.

160
00:10:14,053 --> 00:10:16,410
If you are my enemy,
then fight me like one.

161
00:10:16,493 --> 00:10:19,022
If not, I'll take this
treasure for myself.

162
00:10:20,073 --> 00:10:24,213
So I take it knowing the answer to
that question is your second wish.

163
00:10:24,873 --> 00:10:28,049
Though it's a little on the
boring side if you ask me,

164
00:10:28,273 --> 00:10:31,850
but I owe you a debt of gratitude
for letting me out of that lamp,

165
00:10:31,933 --> 00:10:33,521
so I shall grant your wish.

166
00:10:33,673 --> 00:10:35,497
You know you're a smug bastard.

167
00:10:36,193 --> 00:10:38,134
All right then, have it your way.

168
00:10:38,353 --> 00:10:40,153
I do have a wish.

169
00:10:40,813 --> 00:10:42,673
I want to be a comic artist!

170
00:10:42,913 --> 00:10:44,830
That was always my dream
back when I was a kid.

171
00:10:44,913 --> 00:10:47,130
And don't make me some
pathetic one either!

172
00:10:47,213 --> 00:10:48,930
I want to be bigger than Disney!

173
00:10:49,013 --> 00:10:52,248
In fact, someday I'm gonna
build my own Polnareff land!

174
00:10:53,933 --> 00:10:54,890
Y-you know what?

175
00:10:54,973 --> 00:10:55,990
Scratch that idea.

176
00:10:56,073 --> 00:10:57,790
Just give me a second to think.

177
00:10:57,873 --> 00:11:00,613
Any minute now, it'll come to me...

178
00:11:01,193 --> 00:11:02,450
I've made up my mind!

179
00:11:02,533 --> 00:11:04,298
I want a beautiful girlfriend!

180
00:11:05,473 --> 00:11:06,993
More than money or fame.

181
00:11:07,873 --> 00:11:09,533
What I want is true love!

182
00:11:09,753 --> 00:11:11,670
I'm talking not only
someone who's really cute!

183
00:11:11,753 --> 00:11:13,030
But a girl who wore pinkies for her?

184
00:11:13,113 --> 00:11:14,930
she loves me with all her heart.

185
00:11:15,013 --> 00:11:18,750
I want to meet a girl who feels the
same way about me as I do for her.

186
00:11:18,833 --> 00:11:23,270
So if that's within your power to do,
then prove it to me right now, dammit!

187
00:11:23,353 --> 00:11:26,113
You want a girl, do you? Very well.

188
00:11:26,473 --> 00:11:27,773
Wait, no, never mind.

189
00:11:27,973 --> 00:11:29,973
I need time to think this through.

190
00:11:44,413 --> 00:11:45,653
I have a question.

191
00:11:47,373 --> 00:11:51,053
Do you have the ability to revive someone?

192
00:11:51,853 --> 00:11:53,930
Am I to assume you're wanting to know the

193
00:11:54,013 --> 00:11:56,330
answer to that question
is your second wish?

194
00:11:56,413 --> 00:11:57,243
Cut it out!

195
00:11:57,326 --> 00:12:00,090
I'm asking you to bring my
dead sister back to life.

196
00:12:00,173 --> 00:12:03,150
And while you're at it, you can
do the same for my friend Avdol.

197
00:12:03,233 --> 00:12:06,115
That shouldn't be too much
of a challenge, right?

198
00:12:13,473 --> 00:12:14,573
Very well.

199
00:12:14,953 --> 00:12:16,853
I shall grant your wish.

200
00:12:19,333 --> 00:12:20,753
Are you serious?

201
00:12:37,533 --> 00:12:40,833
So you can really... do it? Indeed.

202
00:12:41,293 --> 00:12:45,999
But know that since you made two wishes,
I'll grant them in the order you asked.

203
00:12:46,293 --> 00:12:49,999
First, I will grant your second
wish to bring back your sister.

204
00:12:50,633 --> 00:12:52,593
Hail to you!

205
00:12:54,973 --> 00:12:55,803
Hey!

206
00:12:55,886 --> 00:12:56,988
Don't just disappear!

207
00:12:57,093 --> 00:13:00,211
Who the hell are you and
why are you even doing this?

208
00:13:10,093 --> 00:13:11,353
What was that sound?

209
00:13:12,213 --> 00:13:14,742
I'm sure I heard
something rustling around.

210
00:13:15,793 --> 00:13:18,734
It sounded like someone
was digging up the ground.

211
00:13:29,473 --> 00:13:31,414
There's that weird digging again.

212
00:13:32,373 --> 00:13:34,197
Where's that sound coming from?

213
00:13:38,813 --> 00:13:40,173
No, impossible.

214
00:13:45,253 --> 00:13:47,973
Wait, is that a woman crying?

215
00:13:49,013 --> 00:13:51,253
All right, who the hell's back here?

216
00:13:52,533 --> 00:13:53,673
These are...

217
00:14:02,993 --> 00:14:06,733
These are strands of hair,
and a woman's hair no less.

218
00:14:07,913 --> 00:14:09,473
A woman's footsteps.

219
00:14:09,893 --> 00:14:10,973
It can't be!

220
00:14:19,493 --> 00:14:22,590
There's no way this can't
be happening, can it?

221
00:14:22,673 --> 00:14:24,133
As far as I know,

222
00:14:24,273 --> 00:14:28,610
my little sister is still in her coffin
back in France, so how could she be?

223
00:14:28,693 --> 00:14:30,222
Just who the hell are you?

224
00:14:30,333 --> 00:14:32,333
You better answer me right now!

225
00:14:34,713 --> 00:14:36,193
Please, stay away.

226
00:14:39,613 --> 00:14:41,153
I'm in so much pain.

227
00:14:42,173 --> 00:14:45,593
My body hasn't fully formed yet.

228
00:14:46,893 --> 00:14:48,453
I know that voice.

229
00:14:54,733 --> 00:14:55,853
Sherry, it's you.

230
00:14:59,393 --> 00:15:00,890
Polnareff's been gone a while.

231
00:15:00,973 --> 00:15:02,267
Where'd he run off to?

232
00:15:02,833 --> 00:15:04,421
I couldn't find him up top.

233
00:15:04,693 --> 00:15:05,850
Where could he have gone?

234
00:15:05,933 --> 00:15:08,610
It's already nightfall and
he's nowhere to be seen.

235
00:15:08,693 --> 00:15:13,164
Do you think that he could have gotten
tangled up in a fight with the enemy?

236
00:15:15,153 --> 00:15:18,013
Sherry, am I hallucinating
or is it really you?

237
00:15:19,933 --> 00:15:21,473
It is you, isn't it?

238
00:15:34,573 --> 00:15:35,403
Wait!

239
00:15:35,486 --> 00:15:36,509
Where are you going?

240
00:15:36,613 --> 00:15:38,260
Where are you going, Cherry?

241
00:15:38,693 --> 00:15:40,281
Wait, Cherry, it's only me!

242
00:15:40,593 --> 00:15:42,534
Cherry, why are you running away?

243
00:15:47,473 --> 00:15:48,393
Where are you?

244
00:15:48,653 --> 00:15:50,050
Come on, Cherry, please!

245
00:15:50,133 --> 00:15:51,550
I'm begging you to show yourself!

246
00:15:51,633 --> 00:15:53,333
Let me see your face!

247
00:15:53,593 --> 00:15:55,240
Let me see it one more time!

248
00:15:57,413 --> 00:15:58,613
Hey, brother!

249
00:16:00,853 --> 00:16:01,933
Higher, brother!

250
00:16:02,393 --> 00:16:04,153
Raise me as high as you can!

251
00:16:05,773 --> 00:16:06,603
Yay!

252
00:16:06,686 --> 00:16:07,773
Now spin me around!

253
00:16:12,753 --> 00:16:14,713
Oh, it's simply wonderful!

254
00:16:15,213 --> 00:16:17,154
I've been wanting a new umbrella!

255
00:16:17,833 --> 00:16:19,833
Thank you for buying it for me!

256
00:16:21,633 --> 00:16:22,753
I'm off now.

257
00:16:34,813 --> 00:16:35,733
Sherry!

258
00:16:37,253 --> 00:16:38,083
Sherry!

259
00:16:41,033 --> 00:16:43,933
Monkyu, what the hell happened here?

260
00:16:45,713 --> 00:16:47,313
They've been half eaten.

261
00:16:54,113 --> 00:16:54,943
Sherry!

262
00:16:55,213 --> 00:16:56,413
Can you hear me?

263
00:16:56,633 --> 00:16:57,870
Why are you running away?

264
00:16:57,953 --> 00:17:00,013
It's me, your big brother!

265
00:17:01,373 --> 00:17:04,033
Because my body is covered in mud.

266
00:17:07,393 --> 00:17:08,733
And there's my hair.

267
00:17:09,073 --> 00:17:10,250
It's so unkempt.

268
00:17:10,333 --> 00:17:11,513
It's okay, Sherry.

269
00:17:11,733 --> 00:17:13,030
Don't worry about that.

270
00:17:13,113 --> 00:17:16,760
You've got to believe me when I
say you're perfect as you are.

271
00:17:19,753 --> 00:17:21,153
Why are you crying?

272
00:17:22,433 --> 00:17:23,813
Sherry, talk to me.

273
00:17:24,073 --> 00:17:25,173
Why are you sad?

274
00:17:39,753 --> 00:17:41,133
Oh, Sherry.

275
00:17:43,633 --> 00:17:44,463
No.

276
00:17:44,546 --> 00:17:45,613
Just stay back.

277
00:17:45,953 --> 00:17:47,293
Don't come any closer.

278
00:17:47,793 --> 00:17:48,969
What are you saying?

279
00:17:49,273 --> 00:17:50,920
You're not making any sense.

280
00:17:53,433 --> 00:17:54,263
It's simple.

281
00:17:54,346 --> 00:17:56,033
I'm saying you'll hate me.

282
00:17:56,233 --> 00:18:00,292
Oh, Sherry, have I ever said anything
to make you think I'd hate you?

283
00:18:00,773 --> 00:18:01,753
Yes, you have.

284
00:18:02,873 --> 00:18:05,050
It was when we were little kids and I gave

285
00:18:05,133 --> 00:18:07,870
your favorite tropical
fish to that stupid cat.

286
00:18:07,953 --> 00:18:11,153
You got really angry over
it and said you hated me.

287
00:18:12,453 --> 00:18:15,373
I admit I was angry that
day, but no matter what,

288
00:18:15,493 --> 00:18:17,970
I've always loved you more
than the stars in the sky,

289
00:18:18,053 --> 00:18:19,073
and I still do.

290
00:18:20,253 --> 00:18:21,083
Really?

291
00:18:21,166 --> 00:18:23,090
You've always loved me,
no matter what I did?

292
00:18:23,173 --> 00:18:24,733
Yes, of course I have.

293
00:18:25,653 --> 00:18:28,050
And does that feeling
hold true to this day?

294
00:18:28,133 --> 00:18:30,427
I will always love you, no matter what.

295
00:18:30,613 --> 00:18:33,410
And I can clearly see now
that you're the real Sherry.

296
00:18:33,493 --> 00:18:36,846
You have no idea how much I've
missed you, little sister.

297
00:18:39,553 --> 00:18:40,383
I see.

298
00:18:40,466 --> 00:18:42,393
I feel the same, big brother.

299
00:18:42,993 --> 00:18:44,713
Sherry, please look this way.

300
00:18:44,953 --> 00:18:48,247
I'm begging you to show me
that beautiful face of yours.

301
00:18:49,913 --> 00:18:51,693
Why are you crying, Cherry?

302
00:18:51,973 --> 00:18:54,213
Are you still sad? Sad?

303
00:18:55,033 --> 00:18:56,113
No, brother.

304
00:18:56,933 --> 00:18:58,773
These are tears of sadness.

305
00:18:59,293 --> 00:19:02,633
I'm crying because...
What? What is it then?

306
00:19:03,733 --> 00:19:04,563
I'm...

307
00:19:05,073 --> 00:19:06,713
I'm happy, brother.

308
00:19:07,913 --> 00:19:10,013
Cause I can finally hit you!

309
00:19:19,693 --> 00:19:21,073
Ch-Cherry Dunn!

310
00:19:32,813 --> 00:19:33,933
Ch-Cherry...

311
00:19:35,333 --> 00:19:37,733
I'm sorry that I bit you, brother.

312
00:19:38,193 --> 00:19:41,253
I'm afraid my body is
still underdeveloped.

313
00:19:42,433 --> 00:19:45,933
But if I eat your flesh,
I'll return to normal.

314
00:19:46,633 --> 00:19:48,733
It's okay if I eat you, right?

315
00:19:49,133 --> 00:19:50,513
What am I saying?

316
00:19:50,873 --> 00:19:53,153
You always did what I asked you to.

317
00:20:01,493 --> 00:20:02,323
Cameo!

318
00:20:04,933 --> 00:20:05,763
You rang?

319
00:20:05,846 --> 00:20:07,053
You bastard!

320
00:20:07,793 --> 00:20:09,373
What's all the fuss about?

321
00:20:09,673 --> 00:20:11,070
Do you have a complaint?

322
00:20:11,153 --> 00:20:13,093
I granted your wish, didn't I?

323
00:20:13,953 --> 00:20:16,393
Granting wishes is my power after all.

324
00:20:16,653 --> 00:20:19,359
What you do with them
is completely up to you.

325
00:20:20,853 --> 00:20:24,513
Then let me use this opportunity
to tell you my third wish.

326
00:20:27,053 --> 00:20:28,733
Make my sister.

327
00:20:32,593 --> 00:20:33,593
Make her.

328
00:20:39,713 --> 00:20:43,753
Make my sister return to her
grave so she can rest in peace!

329
00:20:54,753 --> 00:20:56,733
I don't think so.

330
00:20:58,033 --> 00:20:58,933
Why not?

331
00:20:59,193 --> 00:21:01,670
You still don't get it, do you, Polnareff?

332
00:21:01,753 --> 00:21:04,433
If you haven't figured
it out, I'm a stand.

333
00:21:04,753 --> 00:21:06,093
Not just any stand.

334
00:21:06,293 --> 00:21:08,705
The one represented by the judgment card.

335
00:21:09,373 --> 00:21:10,273
You see,

336
00:21:10,533 --> 00:21:15,250
my powers allow me to extract wishes from
the deepest corners of the human mind.

337
00:21:15,333 --> 00:21:17,693
and manifest it from the soil below.

338
00:21:17,973 --> 00:21:20,738
You created your sister
from your own yearning.

339
00:21:21,393 --> 00:21:22,653
How dare you?

340
00:21:22,833 --> 00:21:26,693
And since you created
her, I cannot undo it.

341
00:21:28,153 --> 00:21:31,253
It looks like the winner
of this battle is me.

342
00:21:35,713 --> 00:21:40,493
By the way, I seem to recall you
saying something about a third wish.

343
00:21:40,853 --> 00:21:42,610
But don't you remember, Polnareff?

344
00:21:42,693 --> 00:21:45,773
You've already made
your third wish. Oh, no.

345
00:21:48,093 --> 00:21:49,873
You don't mean him.

346
00:22:07,813 --> 00:22:10,490
All the old paintings on the tomb.

347
00:22:10,573 --> 00:22:12,530
They do the sand dance, don't you know?

348
00:22:12,613 --> 00:22:14,173
If they move too quick.

349
00:22:14,833 --> 00:22:17,190
They're falling down like a domino.

350
00:22:17,273 --> 00:22:19,850
All the birds are men by the Nile.

351
00:22:19,933 --> 00:22:21,910
They've got their money on a bed.

352
00:22:21,993 --> 00:22:23,510
Called crocodiles.

353
00:22:23,593 --> 00:22:26,490
They snap their teeth on your cigarette.

354
00:22:26,573 --> 00:22:28,813
Falling tight to the hookah. I say.

355
00:22:35,333 --> 00:22:37,713
Walk like an Egyptian.

356
00:22:49,373 --> 00:22:51,090
The blonde waitresses.

357
00:22:51,173 --> 00:22:52,490
Take their trays.

358
00:22:52,573 --> 00:22:54,470
Spin around and they cross the floor.

359
00:22:54,553 --> 00:22:55,990
They've got the moves.

360
00:22:56,073 --> 00:22:57,950
You drop, you drink.

361
00:22:58,033 --> 00:22:59,150
Then they bring you more.

362
00:22:59,233 --> 00:23:01,770
All the school kids so sick of books.

363
00:23:01,853 --> 00:23:03,830
They're like the punk and the metal band.

364
00:23:03,913 --> 00:23:05,310
When the buzzer rings.

365
00:23:05,393 --> 00:23:08,070
They're walking like an Egyptian.

366
00:23:08,153 --> 00:23:11,430
All the kids in the marketplace say. Walk

367
00:23:11,513 --> 00:23:18,513
like

368
00:23:18,893 --> 00:23:19,723
an Egyptian.

369
00:23:22,633 --> 00:23:25,390
When a man uncovers his deepest desires.

370
00:23:25,473 --> 00:23:27,710
All of his weaknesses are laid bare.

371
00:23:27,793 --> 00:23:29,910
Because of your idiotic, bumbling eye!

372
00:23:29,993 --> 00:23:32,490
After all, I truly didn't
think you'd be this hurt.

373
00:23:32,573 --> 00:23:34,455
I'll get better if I eat, right?

374
00:23:34,993 --> 00:23:37,373
I know it was only the third wish.
